Paper batch 3 of round 3: Claude Opus 5.5 as definition-item writer (H-c, H1 and H2) judged, staged beside H-a and written into the paper

Stage runs/stage7_round3 again from the raw runs (analysis code 4cc8db5, clean): h_opus.json is block
H for the Claude Opus 5.5 definition-item writer, read with its response-cache snapshot (SHA256 in the
manifest); u, u_delta, n, y and h_sonnet differ only in the code field. Commit the manifests, env and
hash checks of the five H-c runs. RThreeHOpus macros and the H1/H2 (Opus) rows of tab_round3
generated; tests pin the Opus verdicts and values, the H-c trigger recorded in h_sonnet.json and the
equal point estimate the text states once for both writers.

Verdicts: H-c valid (944 distinct writes, 0 at the output limit, 0 unreadable, longest 2,118 output
tokens; 10,080 anchor answers reproduced). H1 for Opus reads both (B x D after S_def +16.4 pp
[+9.8, +23.0]; +23.6 pp after S_src, +30.5 pp after S_del). H2 holds (r_0 43.0% [32.9, 51.1], +30.3 pp
[+22.7, +37.8] over Qwen3.5-9B's 12.7% on the same item-times). Opus's B x D after S_def has the same
point estimate as Sonnet's (33 of 201 item-times net each), but 18 of the 201 item-level values differ.

Paper: abstract (rephrased, no added sentence, 318 words against 319), introduction bullet, 4.2
paragraph, rule 2 and the Models limitation report both writers; appendix B (models, registration
status, round-3 subsection, readings and deviations tables), the license paragraph and the
reproducibility statement name Opus 5.5 with its settings. Construct limitation shortened so the
main text still ends on page 9.

